      "id": 1,
      "text": "Weedville sits in the Bennett Branch Sinnemahoning Creek valley, southeast of Elk County.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Weedville%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "location_description"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Pennsylvania Route 255 cuts through Weedville, linking it 12 miles north to St. Marys and 19 miles south to DuBois.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13,
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Weedville%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "location_description"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The town’s name echoes early settler William H. Bennett, who logged the area and lent his name to Bennett’s Branch.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16,
        17,
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://mtzionhistoricalsociety.org/visit/visit-elk-county/",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Logging once dominated Weedville, with log rafts flowing down Bennett’s Branch, earning nearby Williamsport the title of the nation’s lumber capital.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21,
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://mtzionhistoricalsociety.org/visit/visit-elk-county/",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Coal mining later scarred the landscape, but recent reclamation projects have cleaned streams and restored former strip‑mine sites.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23,
        24,
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://mtzionhistoricalsociety.org/visit/visit-elk-county/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Today, Bennett’s Valley hosts a thriving elk population, with estimates of 1,200 animals roaming the hills and attracting wildlife enthusiasts.",
